---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Button from "./Button.astro";
import Eyebrow from "./Eyebrow.astro";
import octagonExplained from "../assets/heritage/turathi-octogan-explained.jpeg";
---

<section class="bg-navy text-paper naqsh-light">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24">
    <Eyebrow>The Turathi Octagon</Eyebrow>
    <h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl sm:text-3xl">What it is</h2>
    <span class="mt-4 block h-px w-16 bg-brass"></span>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-paper/75">
      The Turathi Octagon is how I honour restaurants that embody the finest
      traditions of their cuisine and heritage. Tradition isn't nostalgia. It's
      the better answer we stopped using.
    </p>

    {/* The Octagon explained: three tiers, one to three stars. */}
    <Image
      src={octagonExplained}
      alt="The Turathi Octagon explained: Fine Cooking is one star for cooking well made and rooted in tradition, Distinguished Table is two stars for a vivid sense of place, Cultural Landmark is three stars for a living expression of its heritage"
      widths={[500, 800, 1024]}
      sizes="(max-width: 768px) 92vw, 60vw"
      class="mt-10 h-auto w-full max-w-3xl border-t-2 border-brass shadow-sm"
    />

    <div class="mt-12">
      <Button href="/the-turathi-octagon" variant="light-outline">Explore the Octagon</Button>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
